Exercise 1: Create a Dockerfile for a new image that starts from ubuntu:24.04 and add instructions to install curl into that image.
Then add instructions to copy the script file into that image and finally set it to run on container start using CMD.
........Create a shell sript named bday.sh
#!/bin/bash
while true
do
  echo "Input website:"
  read website; echo "Searching.."
  sleep 1; curl http://$website
done
........Create a docker file named Dockerfile.curl
FROM ubuntu:24.04

WORKDIR /app

COPY bday.sh .

RUN chmod +x bday.sh

RUN apt-get update

RUN apt install -y curl 

#RUN apt-get update && apt install -y curl # this can be written multiple line or one line

CMD ["./bday.sh"]
